    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0970" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg958"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/3–1346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-13T20:00:00-05:00">March 13, 1946—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2266. Brit withdrawal requirement free rice contribution by Siam of which Dept
                    informed subsequent to Instruction 6475 Mar 4 greatly decreases need formal
                    Allied Claims Commission. Dept giving further consideration its suggestion
                    (Deptel 2135, Mar 8<anchor n="26" xml:id="d747-f1"/>) that uniform principles
                    should be applicable all Allied claims in view complicated French and Chinese
                    situation.</p>
                <p>Dept now considers it might be better withdraw suggestion (Deptel 2135, Mar 8)
                    and also not to establish Allied Claims Commission but provide for informal
                    understanding between Brit, US, Australia and possibly Dutch on principles
                    governing appropriate categories, evaluation and settlement their claims along
                    general lines indicated Instructions <pb facs="0971" n="959" xml:id="pg959"/>
                    6475, Mar 4. Please discuss immediately FonOff and ascertain their views.<anchor
                        n="27" xml:id="d747-f2"/> Sent London, repeated Bangkok.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d747-f1" n="26" xml:id="d747-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d747-f2" n="27" xml:id="d747-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 2325, March 15, 6 p.m., the Department authorized London to inform
                    the British Foreign Office that “no formal Allied Claims Commission now
                    necessary”. (740.00119 PW/3–1546) Telegram 3083, March 16, 11 a.m., from London
                    reported the concurrence of the Foreign Office and pointed out that the “British
                    might wish to set up some Anglo-Siamese body to deal only with British claims”.
                    (740.00119 PW/3–1646)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
